      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A patient with non-Q wave myocardial infarction had severe luminal narrowing in the first major septal perforator branch, which arose anomalously from the first diagonal branch. In this case, an exercise ECG showed a transient leftward QRS axis shift."},
